WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:06.034
And so the first sermon was about speaking, teaching to speak.

2
00:00:06.034 --> 00:00:09.034
Learn to speak differently than the world speaks.

3
00:00:09.034 --> 00:00:14.034
Coarse language, silly jokes, gossiping about people, saying foolish things.

4
00:00:14.034 --> 00:00:19.034
Unlearn that, because with the same tongue that we occasionally use to glorify God,

5
00:00:19.034 --> 00:00:21.034
we also sometimes use that same tongue for useless talk.

6
00:00:21.034 --> 00:00:23.034
We simply need to unlearn that.

7
00:00:23.034 --> 00:00:28.034
We need to learn to stop saying foolish things and learn to say the right things.

8
00:00:28.034 --> 00:00:29.034
That was sermon 1.

9
00:00:29.034 --> 00:00:37.034
Sermon 2 was something that God has been working on in my own life for quite some time.

10
00:00:37.034 --> 00:00:44.034
And that is, I have felt a kind of revelation and a calling from God to glorify God in the morning.

11
00:00:44.034 --> 00:00:49.034
For a long time now, I have been reading the Bible in a structured way.

12
00:00:49.034 --> 00:00:52.034
That means I read a piece of the Bible every day.

13
00:00:52.034 --> 00:00:56.034
And then I write the S in my notebook, which means scripture underneath.

14
00:00:56.034 --> 00:01:01.034
And then I write down which Bible verse from the chapter I read that day,

15
00:01:01.034 --> 00:01:04.034
which verse stood out the most.

16
00:01:04.034 --> 00:01:07.034
I write that down, I quote that verse.

17
00:01:07.034 --> 00:01:10.034
Below that, I write the letter O, which means observation.

18
00:01:10.034 --> 00:01:13.034
What do I think that means?

19
00:01:13.034 --> 00:01:15.034
I write that out in a few words.

20
00:01:15.034 --> 00:01:17.034
I don't have much patience; it's always brief.

21
00:01:17.034 --> 00:01:21.034
I put the letter A underneath it, application.

22
00:01:21.034 --> 00:01:24.034
What does it mean, but what does it mean in my life?

23
00:01:24.034 --> 00:01:27.034
What am I going to do with it?

24
00:01:27.034 --> 00:01:30.034
Because when you read the story of Ezra, which we are going to read shortly,

25
00:01:30.034 --> 00:01:34.034
when you read the story of David, when you read the story of Jesus,

26
00:01:34.034 --> 00:01:36.034
what can I do with that? That is so important.

27
00:01:36.034 --> 00:01:40.034
You can read the Word, but you also have to put it into action. Amen?

28
00:01:40.034 --> 00:01:43.034
And then finally I write the letter P, prayer.

29
00:01:43.034 --> 00:01:49.034
Then I pray that God can help me to carry out what His will is from His Word.

30
00:01:49.034 --> 00:01:54.034
And every day I do that for a very long time now.

31
00:01:54.034 --> 00:02:00.034
And then I get up in the morning and I read that and I write that and then I pray a little.

32
00:02:00.034 --> 00:02:04.034
But God has asked something of me recently.

33
00:02:04.034 --> 00:02:07.034
And He said to me, Tim, do you want to make me great too?

34
00:02:07.034 --> 00:02:11.034
Heart open in your own room where no one is present.

35
00:02:11.034 --> 00:02:16.034
And actually you might think to yourself, that's a no-brainer, everyone does that.

36
00:02:16.034 --> 00:02:21.034
Well, for a long time I did pray, I read the Word, I love the group of people to come together,

37
00:02:21.034 --> 00:02:25.034
to worship and then I am loud. I am actually always loud.

38
00:02:25.034 --> 00:02:30.034
But in that part of my personal, in my private devotion, I was not so loud.

39
00:02:30.034 --> 00:02:34.034
And God said to me, make me great. With words of praise.

40
00:02:34.034 --> 00:02:41.034
And He gave me insight to go through the Psalms and to study the Psalms.

41
00:02:41.034 --> 00:02:45.034
This psalm stands for this. David wrote various songs.

42
00:02:45.034 --> 00:02:49.034
And one song was, for example, to ask for forgiveness from God.

43
00:02:49.034 --> 00:02:53.034
Another song is when he is in trouble and then says, God come to my aid.

44
00:02:53.034 --> 00:02:57.034
Another song is when he is among his enemies and then says, what should I do here among those enemies?

45
00:02:57.034 --> 00:03:03.034
At another moment he writes a song where he thinks that God gives no answer at the moment he asks something.

46
00:03:03.034 --> 00:03:07.034
How many of the people in this room have ever dealt with that?

47
00:03:07.034 --> 00:03:10.034
That you pray for something and think you receive no answer.

48
00:03:10.034 --> 00:03:12.034
And all hands went up.

49
00:03:12.034 --> 00:03:15.034
God can sometimes be eerily silent.

50
00:03:15.034 --> 00:03:18.034
And there is a reason for that.

51
00:03:18.034 --> 00:03:23.034
For God does not play hide and seek. God is also not annoying.

52
00:03:23.034 --> 00:03:26.034
But God's will is higher than your will.

53
00:03:26.034 --> 00:03:31.034
And David writes from his emotions, Lord, wake up.

54
00:03:31.034 --> 00:03:34.034
I am here in trouble and you seem to be sleeping.

55
00:03:34.034 --> 00:03:36.034
And those are the different psalms.

56
00:03:37.034 --> 00:03:46.034
But through those 150 psalms there are also worship psalms.

57
00:03:46.034 --> 00:03:48.034
Worship psalms.

58
00:03:48.034 --> 00:03:51.034
Praise psalms.

59
00:03:51.034 --> 00:03:54.034
And God recently asked me, some time ago.

60
00:03:54.034 --> 00:04:05.034
He said, Tim, read every day when you get up early in the morning and you have read your Bible and made your notes and you have prayed.

61
00:04:05.034 --> 00:04:14.034
Then add a short worship, a worship by reading one of those worship psalms.

62
00:04:14.034 --> 00:04:17.034
And do it as David says.

63
00:04:17.034 --> 00:04:22.034
For David also says, I love to worship You with my hands raised high.

64
00:04:22.034 --> 00:04:24.034
Okay, if David does it, then I will do it too.

65
00:04:24.034 --> 00:04:29.034
And then you take your basic Bible or your international Bible, it doesn't matter which Bible.

66
00:04:29.034 --> 00:04:36.034
And so I start from that time, I start to magnify God and I begin to read a psalm out loud.

67
00:04:36.034 --> 00:04:43.034
Do you know why? Because I believe that God has clothed me with authority.

68
00:04:46.034 --> 00:04:51.034
Imagine, men, women, everyone, clothed with the name of Jesus.

69
00:04:51.034 --> 00:04:57.034
Just imagine what will happen to the city in which we live.

70
00:04:57.034 --> 00:05:01.034
The habitat where God has placed you.

71
00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:07.034
Now just imagine if 100% of the church would do this.

72
00:05:07.034 --> 00:05:14.034
That when the sun rises, the morning dew is there, the birds are just starting to sing.

73
00:05:14.034 --> 00:05:17.034
And those birds give glory to God, they cannot do otherwise.

74
00:05:17.034 --> 00:05:20.034
They give glory to God as soon as they open their mouths.

75
00:05:20.034 --> 00:05:22.034
The trees cannot do otherwise.

76
00:05:22.034 --> 00:05:26.034
They are already raising their hands to magnify God.

77
00:05:26.034 --> 00:05:30.034
The trees cannot do otherwise, the birds cannot do otherwise, the animals cannot do otherwise.

78
00:05:30.034 --> 00:05:36.034
And the whole earth wakes up in Lommel on my morning in which I am placed.

79
00:05:36.034 --> 00:05:41.034
The animals cannot do otherwise, the stones cannot do otherwise, the sun cannot do otherwise.

80
00:05:41.034 --> 00:05:44.034
The clouds cannot do otherwise, the birds cannot do otherwise.

81
00:05:44.034 --> 00:05:50.034
But in the morning glory, God, the Creator of heaven and earth, asks Tim Lauré.

82
00:05:50.034 --> 00:05:55.034
Will you also open your mouth to worship me? Yes Lord, gladly.

83
00:05:55.034 --> 00:06:01.034
And there you stand in your greenhouse, thank you Lord, and then you read a psalm.

84
00:06:01.034 --> 00:06:08.034
And my challenge on Saturday morning was, guys, can I invite you, can I challenge you

85
00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:13.034
to join in speaking such a praise psalm.

86
00:06:13.034 --> 00:06:15.034
And we quickly went through those psalms.

87
00:06:15.034 --> 00:06:19.034
This psalm, that psalm, that psalm, I can name them.

88
00:06:20.034 --> 00:06:23.034
No, I won't do that now, you should have been there.

89
00:06:26.034 --> 00:06:31.034
And I truly believe, church, I believe with all that is in me.

90
00:06:32.034 --> 00:06:40.034
That changes are going to come in your family, in your marriage, in your personal life, in your health,

91
00:06:41.034 --> 00:06:51.034
in your financial situation, and even if your financial situation changes, lack of sleep.

92
00:06:51.034 --> 00:06:58.034
And even if your financial situation does not change, your perspective on your financial situation will still change.

93
00:06:59.034 --> 00:07:05.034
By magnifying God, your eyes are drawn to Him, and no longer to that financial situation.

94
00:07:05.034 --> 00:07:07.034
It doesn't matter how much money you have.

95
00:07:08.034 --> 00:07:13.034
If you look to the provider, if you look to the Supplier, then you know that what you have,

96
00:07:13.034 --> 00:07:19.034
that you will receive wisdom from Him and provision for what you need to do, that is what this sermon is about.

97
00:07:20.034 --> 00:07:22.034
Men, one more time I want to challenge you.

98
00:07:22.034 --> 00:07:26.034
Men who have been to the men's camp, and also men who have not been to the men's camp.

99
00:07:27.034 --> 00:07:34.034
May I challenge you, please, to stand in the authority that God has given you.

100
00:07:34.034 --> 00:07:40.034
You are kings and priests, appointed over the earth to reign in the name of Jesus.

101
00:07:41.034 --> 00:07:43.034
This is really not arrogance or chauvinism, really not.

102
00:07:44.034 --> 00:07:47.034
This is what God has said from the beginning to Adam.

103
00:07:47.034 --> 00:07:53.034
Here Adam, here is my creation. Rule over it.

104
00:07:53.034 --> 00:07:58.034
But through sin, something has broken, there is a distance between God and man,

105
00:07:58.034 --> 00:08:01.034
and thus also the authority that man had over creation.

106
00:08:01.034 --> 00:08:08.034
But in the name of Jesus, washed by the blood of Jesus and covered with the mantle of righteousness,

107
00:08:08.034 --> 00:08:14.034
we are again in the commission of Adam to reign over the place where you live.

108
00:08:14.034 --> 00:08:19.034
Why do you think you live where you live? Do you think you chose it yourself?

109
00:08:19.034 --> 00:08:27.034
No way. God has placed you there. Really? Did God place me here, in that strange neighborhood where I live?

110
00:08:27.034 --> 00:08:35.034
Yes, God has placed you there. In that strange neighborhood where you live, with all those problems where you live,

111
00:08:35.034 --> 00:08:41.034
with so few Christians where you live, you have been chosen to live there.

112
00:08:41.034 --> 00:08:46.034
And just imagine, men, that when we get up in the morning and the sun rises,

113
00:08:46.034 --> 00:08:52.034
and we shout it out, from the north to the south, from the west to the east,

114
00:08:52.034 --> 00:08:58.034
and we proclaim only the praises of God, just imagine the power that is released then.

115
00:08:58.034 --> 00:09:07.034
Lovely. When men stand up, sermon 1, in their speech, how we speak, that we learn to speak like Jesus.

116
00:09:07.034 --> 00:09:15.034
Step 2, that we learn to praise, worship, morning praises, or if you are an evening person, do it in the evening too.

117
00:09:15.034 --> 00:09:21.034
Before you lie down flat, sit on the edge of your bed, or kneel by your bed, and do exactly the same.

118
00:09:21.034 --> 00:09:27.034
For it doesn't matter if you do it at morning glory or at sunset, it really doesn't matter.

119
00:09:27.034 --> 00:09:30.034
Make God great.

120
00:09:31.034 --> 00:09:37.034
And my last sermon last night was very simple, also learn to pray, in the name of Jesus.

121
00:09:37.034 --> 00:09:44.034
You pray. Men, do not expect it from your women. Do not let the women take authority,

122
00:09:44.034 --> 00:09:49.034
and I do not say this in a wrong way, but why are men passive,

123
00:09:49.034 --> 00:09:54.034
and do we think, oh those women will solve it, in the authority of my house.

124
00:09:54.034 --> 00:09:59.034
No, says Joshua, but I and my household, we will serve the Lord.

125
00:09:59.034 --> 00:10:02.034
So Joshua knows what his mandate is.

126
00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:07.034
Here is a tip to all fathers, do not be intimidated by your children.

127
00:10:07.034 --> 00:10:15.034
What you say needs to happen in the family to glorify God, that must happen in the family to glorify God.

128
00:10:15.034 --> 00:10:20.034
If your teenagers say, yes but I want to go this way, then you as a man can say,

129
00:10:20.034 --> 00:10:25.034
yes but listen, this is what God's Word says, and we will serve God this way.

130
00:10:25.034 --> 00:10:29.034
Whatever you think about it, because your children can rebel anyway.

131
00:10:29.034 --> 00:10:34.034
And if you are afraid of that, then you take the passive step, while God has said,

132
00:10:34.034 --> 00:10:39.034
but you men must stand in the authority that God has for you.

133
00:10:39.034 --> 00:10:44.034
And so also learn to pray, and at the end of last night's nice camp,

134
00:10:44.034 --> 00:10:47.034
we just prayed for each other, and do you know how beautiful it is.

135
00:10:47.034 --> 00:10:53.034
And do you know how proud the Father in heaven is when He sees His sons praying with each other.

136
00:10:53.034 --> 00:10:59.034
It was beautiful to our eyes, let alone how beautiful it is for the Father.

137
00:10:59.034 --> 00:11:00.034
So beautiful.

138
00:11:00.034 --> 00:11:06.034
And this Sunday morning I want to conclude, so we have talked about speaking in authority,

139
00:11:06.034 --> 00:11:12.034
we have talked about worship in authority, we have talked about praying in authority,

140
00:11:12.034 --> 00:11:16.034
and the last sermon is a mix of what I have experienced this past week,

141
00:11:16.034 --> 00:11:19.034
together with the board and the leadership of Open Church,

142
00:11:19.034 --> 00:11:24.034
and something that I have received as a sign from God, at least that is how I feel it has been,

143
00:11:24.034 --> 00:11:28.034
and also as a message to the men and also the women.

144
00:11:28.034 --> 00:11:33.034
If you have a Bible with you, please turn with me to Ezra, chapter 7.

145
00:11:37.034 --> 00:11:39.034
Ezra, chapter 7.

146
00:11:40.034 --> 00:11:51.034
Ezra, chapter 7, is about the fact that Ezra and Nehemiah are returning from Babylon to Judea,

147
00:11:51.034 --> 00:11:56.034
to rebuild the city of Jerusalem and to rebuild the temple of the Lord.

148
00:11:56.034 --> 00:11:58.034
Here is the story.

149
00:11:58.034 --> 00:12:05.034
Because of the sin of the people, decay has come over the land.

150
00:12:06.034 --> 00:12:10.034
If we could just pause and reflect on that, right?

151
00:12:10.034 --> 00:12:14.034
Because of the sin of the people, problems arise in the land.

152
00:12:16.034 --> 00:12:20.034
I repeat, because of the sin of the people, problems arise in the land.

153
00:12:24.034 --> 00:12:28.034
If there is a God, you hear in the world, why does He not do anything about it?

154
00:12:28.034 --> 00:12:32.034
If there is a God, why do you listen to Him, yes?

155
00:12:33.034 --> 00:12:39.034
For if we had listened to the laws of God, we would have had a beautiful heaven and earth.

156
00:12:39.034 --> 00:12:43.034
But because of the sin of the people, decay comes into the land.

157
00:12:43.034 --> 00:12:49.034
And God can even use a Babylonian king, like Nebuchadnezzar,

158
00:12:49.034 --> 00:12:52.034
to say, yes, but we will not proceed like this.

159
00:12:53.034 --> 00:13:02.034
And God sends Nebuchadnezzar to the people to take them away to a foreign land.

160
00:13:02.034 --> 00:13:04.034
A land of idols.

161
00:13:04.034 --> 00:13:07.034
A worldly pagan land.

162
00:13:07.034 --> 00:13:11.034
With the most occult ways of working.

163
00:13:11.034 --> 00:13:19.034
And this story here, about 530 years before Christ approximately,

164
00:13:19.034 --> 00:13:24.034
don't pin me down on the year, we'll pick that up shortly.

165
00:13:24.034 --> 00:13:30.034
We are going to read a part of Ezra chapter 7 shortly, or various parts of it.

166
00:13:30.034 --> 00:13:40.034
But before I do that, I need to touch on the theme of the year.

167
00:13:40.034 --> 00:13:43.034
And what we are doing together as a church.

168
00:13:43.034 --> 00:13:47.034
I want to take you into a piece of relationship that we have with God as a church.

169
00:13:47.034 --> 00:13:50.034
For God is a living God, amen?

170
00:13:50.034 --> 00:13:53.034
God is a living God and He speaks to His family.

171
00:13:53.034 --> 00:13:58.034
He speaks to His people and He is working with us just as He was working with the people in the Bible.

172
00:13:58.034 --> 00:14:02.034
He is an eternal God and He is the same yesterday, today, and tomorrow.

173
00:14:02.034 --> 00:14:04.034
He will always be the same.

174
00:14:04.034 --> 00:14:09.034
So the living God that you see in the Bible, that is the same living God in your personal life.

175
00:14:09.034 --> 00:14:11.034
Okay, here goes the story.

176
00:14:11.034 --> 00:14:14.034
Last Tuesday, so let's set this aside for a moment.

177
00:14:14.034 --> 00:14:16.034
And then you go with me to last Tuesday.

178
00:14:16.034 --> 00:14:23.034
Last Tuesday I had a meeting with the board of Open Church about the construction project.

179
00:14:23.034 --> 00:14:26.034
About the new construction project of Open Church.

180
00:14:26.034 --> 00:14:29.034
As everyone knows in the room, we are saving up.

181
00:14:29.034 --> 00:14:32.034
Are we getting ready to tear down the old building.

182
00:14:32.034 --> 00:14:34.034
To build a new building.

183
00:14:34.034 --> 00:14:36.034
To build a children's church there.

184
00:14:36.034 --> 00:14:41.034
Because God wants more people to be added to the believers.

185
00:14:41.034 --> 00:14:43.034
Because Jesus is coming back, amen?

186
00:14:43.034 --> 00:14:48.034
And before Jesus returns, as many people as possible must have turned to Jesus.

187
00:14:48.034 --> 00:14:50.034
To come to repentance to Jesus.

188
00:14:50.034 --> 00:14:55.034
And God uses this church and many other churches in this area.

189
00:14:55.034 --> 00:14:57.034
For His glory.

190
00:14:57.034 --> 00:15:00.034
But for that, we simply need a new building.

191
00:15:00.034 --> 00:15:07.034
And last year when we started planning this new building, we went to an architect.

192
00:15:07.034 --> 00:15:09.034
We made our plans known.

193
00:15:09.034 --> 00:15:11.034
And here is one thing I want to say in advance.

194
00:15:11.034 --> 00:15:15.034
The plans we have made known are not expensive plans.

195
00:15:15.034 --> 00:15:21.034
The building we have outlined is not going to be built with marble stones and precious stones in the foundation.

196
00:15:21.034 --> 00:15:23.034
It is just a basic building.

197
00:15:23.034 --> 00:15:26.034
It is just a hall and it is basic.

198
00:15:26.034 --> 00:15:28.034
We are not approaching it expensively.

199
00:15:28.034 --> 00:15:34.034
But you know, in the time we live in, it is simply expensive.

200
00:15:34.034 --> 00:15:36.034
Life is simply expensive.

201
00:15:36.034 --> 00:15:38.034
Isolation is expensive.

202
00:15:38.034 --> 00:15:41.034
Signatures from officials are very expensive.

203
00:15:41.034 --> 00:15:43.034
And they are very strict.

204
00:15:43.034 --> 00:15:48.034
And that signature only comes if you say yes sir no sir.

205
00:15:48.034 --> 00:15:51.034
And so this society in which we live is expensive.

206
00:15:51.034 --> 00:15:54.034
And you know, tomorrow is even more expensive than today.

207
00:15:54.034 --> 00:16:01.034
And tomorrow new standards will come along and new insulation standards and new environmental laws and new building regulations.

208
00:16:01.034 --> 00:16:04.034
And it gets more expensive and it gets more expensive and it gets more expensive.

209
00:16:04.034 --> 00:16:08.034
And in our first meeting we had with the architect, the architect asked me.

210
00:16:08.034 --> 00:16:10.034
How much do you think you want to build?

211
00:16:10.034 --> 00:16:12.034
I think one and a half million maybe.

212
00:16:12.034 --> 00:16:13.034
I don't know.

213
00:16:13.034 --> 00:16:15.034
But that was for the shell construction and I really meant that.

214
00:16:15.034 --> 00:16:17.034
Yes, the shell construction one and a half million.

215
00:16:17.034 --> 00:16:24.034
And maybe we would somewhat come close to that one and a half million for shell construction.

216
00:16:24.034 --> 00:16:27.034
But that's not all there is to it.

217
00:16:27.034 --> 00:16:30.034
Because then the government says yes but if you do this then you also have to do that.

218
00:16:30.034 --> 00:16:33.034
And then you have to do that and then you have to do that.

219
00:16:33.034 --> 00:16:34.034
And then you have to do that and then you have to do that.

220
00:16:34.034 --> 00:16:36.034
Yes but I don't want to do that but you have to do it.

221
00:16:36.034 --> 00:16:38.034
And that must, must, must, must, must.

222
00:16:38.034 --> 00:16:42.034
And all of a sudden the number doubles and we are at a project of three million.

223
00:16:45.034 --> 00:16:49.034
